    {
      "id": "motor-v5-smart-11w",
      "name": "V5 Smart Motor (11W)",
      "family": "motor",
      "kind": "model",
      "source": {
        "repo": "vex-cad-download",
        "path": "Motors/V5 Smart Motor (276-4840).step"
      },
      "material": "electronics",
      "snap": "ruled-bores",
      "budgetTriangles": 2000,
      "maxErrorMm": 1.5,
      "boreRule": {
        "minDiameterMm": 2.0,
        "maxDiameterMm": 2.6,
        "minDepthMm": 30
      },
      "notes": [
        "Snap points for the four mounting holes are hand corrections: the 2.2 mm bores through the motor body, found by the bore detector. Their openings are not on the bounding box, so the automatic opening test does not select them. They are 8-32 threaded holes (VEX mounting guide), so they take 8-32 screws only; the STEP's 2.2 mm is the modelled minor diameter.",
        "The output socket is a hand-placed opening at the top of the output boss, where the STEP's 10.3 mm counterbore opens (manual). Its shafts are 1/8 in and 1/4 in square, per VEX's knowledge base; the STEP does not show the square socket cleanly, so only the opening's position and mouth are measured."
      ],
      "snapAccepts": [
        "screw:8-32"
      ],
      "extraSnaps": [
        {
          "kind": "hole",
          "position": [
            12.7,
            0,
            34.0
          ],
          "axis": [
            0,
            0,
            1
          ],
          "diameterMm": 10.3,
          "accepts": [
            "shaft:1/8",
            "shaft:1/4"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
